WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:05.680
Between movies, TV shows, and of course, comics,
there’s more superhero media than ever and

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:09.559
unfortunately for our favorite comic book
characters, that comes with a pretty high

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:10.060
body count.

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:14.419
They might come back after a few years, but
in the meantime, we’re taking a moment to

00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:15.640
remember their loss.

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:21.780
From obscure alternate universes to shockingly
short-lived movie stars, and all the way to

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:26.620
everyone’s favorite super-powered dog, here
are some superheroes we've lost in 2018.

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:28.160
Half of the Avengers

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:34.070
Let's talk about the Thanos in the room: Avengers:
Infinity War ended with the darkest cliffhanger

00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:35.420
in Marvel history.

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:39.420
"You should have gone for the head."

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:46.840
It's devastating… and much more horrific
than the comic book source material, where

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:48.520
people just blinked out of existence.

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:53.740
On the big screen, they feel what's coming
before it hits, and they're slowly erased

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:55.980
inch by inch until there's nothing left.

00:00:56.620 --> 00:01:02.700
By the time the credits roll we watch Bucky,
Falcon, Scarlet Witch, Black Panther, Spider-Man,

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:08.260
Groot, Star-Lord, Drax, Mantis, and Doctor
Strange all get erased from reality.

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:13.500
In the film's one and only post-credits scene,
we see similar fates befall Maria Hill and

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:14.020
Nick Fury.

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:19.080
With sequels in the works for many of these
heroes, it's a safe bet that not all of these

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:20.640
dusty deaths will stick.

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:25.480
But if they do get reversed, it likely won't
be until next year's Avengers sequel and we

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:28.220
won't know until then who will come back and
who won't.

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:29.760
The Mighty Scragg

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:35.060
In 2017’s Venomverse, the Marvel Multiverse
was introduced to an alien race called the

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:39.260
Poisons who were hunting down venom symbiotes
from alternate realities.

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:44.640
This year, they hit Marvel’s Earth in an
event called Venomized, and set their sights

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:46.020
on... the Mighty Scragg?

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:52.250
Scragg was a product of Kid Kaiju, a super-powered
inhuman introduced during the Monsters Unleashed

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:56.220
crossover, who had the power to summon gigantic
monsters by drawing them.

00:01:56.820 --> 00:02:03.420
Scragg, one of Kaiju's creations, was an insectoid
giant who became infected by the Poison during

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:04.080
their invasion.

00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:09.580
Scragg went on a rampage, and while the infection
could be stopped by the symbiote-based hero

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:13.860
Anti-Venom, removing the parasites from him
had lethal consequences.

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:19.090
Without any choice, the heroes did what they
had to do, and Scragg died... but not before

00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:21.300
telling Kid Kaiju that he loved him.

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:22.980
Hey, we’re not crying!

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:23.680
You’re crying!

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:25.020
Robert Brink

00:02:25.420 --> 00:02:29.940
The six-part miniseries New Challengers is
a reimagining of the Silver Age Challengers

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:30.800
of the Unknown.

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:36.120
Unlike earlier incarnations of the characters,
however, the quartet in this series aren’t

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:37.060
superheroic adventurers.

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:39.940
Instead, they’re essentially post-mortem
prisoners.

00:02:40.690 --> 00:02:46.600
Trina Alvarez, Moses Barber, Robert Brink,
and a big guy who goes by "Krunch" all appear

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:51.580
before a mysterious benefactor called Prof
and are told they’ve all just died.

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:55.860
Before he can get any further into explaining
the premise, though, one of the Challengers

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:58.640
dies before he even goes on his first mission.

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:03.480
Robert Brink gets a little too impatient and
hops in a portal, and immediately begins to

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:03.980
melt.

00:03:04.220 --> 00:03:08.140
Whenever the Challengers leave their base
of operations known only as "The Mountain,"

00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:12.780
they're on borrowed time, and if they’re
gone too long, they’ll share Brink’s fate.

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:16.700
Seconds after his death, we meet his replacement:
Bethany Hopkins.

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:22.370
With that, we get our actual team of New Challengers,
who will probably listen a little more carefully

00:03:22.370 --> 00:03:23.220
than poor Robert.

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:24.580
X-Force

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:29.640
In spite of being featured in the trailers
for Deadpool 2, Bedlam was the first member

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:33.580
of X-Force to kick the bucket, and didn’t
even get the chance to throw a punch before

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:34.080
it happened.

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:39.160
Played by Terry Crews, Bedlam is part of the
X-Force team that Deadpool puts together for

00:03:39.160 --> 00:03:41.600
a high-stakes airdrop onto a prison convoy.

00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:47.680
When high speed winds blow them off course,
the entire roster of X-Force aside from Deadpool

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:52.270
and Domino are killed and Bedlam’s blown
face-first into a bus.

00:03:52.270 --> 00:03:56.820
In the darkly hilarious carnage that followed,
the most surprising death was Shatterstar.

00:03:57.140 --> 00:04:02.140
A long-time X-Force member in the comics,
Shatterstar was heavily featured in the trailers,

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:05.820
but sadly wound up on the wrong end of a helicopter
and got chopped to pieces.

00:04:06.460 --> 00:04:09.040
Moviegoers didn’t even get to see his cool
swords!

00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:10.320
They have two blades!

00:04:10.780 --> 00:04:11.780
Next was the Vanisher.

00:04:12.220 --> 00:04:17.160
He was one of the X-Men’s earliest comic
book villains, but when he showed up (or didn’t)

00:04:17.170 --> 00:04:22.760
in Deadpool 2, no one was really sure if Telford
Porter, the teleporting mutant with what might

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:26.160
be the worst name in comics history, actually
existed.

00:04:26.560 --> 00:04:30.860
Eventually, though, it turned out that he
was a full-fledged member of the team, and

00:04:30.860 --> 00:04:35.080
moviegoers got a glimpse at just who was behind
his less-than-visible presence.

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:38.960
"really!?"

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:42.280
As his parachute strayed into electrical wires,
we actually got to see the Vanisher just as

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:46.220
he was being electrocuted, with the unmistakable
face of Brad Pitt.

00:04:46.530 --> 00:04:51.320
In the comics, Zeitgeist is the leader of
a reality-show celebrity version of X-Force

00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:56.040
who dies in the same issue where he makes
his first appearance, so if nothing else,

00:04:56.280 --> 00:04:59.880
Deadpool 2 has that bit of accuracy to its
source material going for it.

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:06.180
Also accurate: his extremely gross super-power
of barfing acid, which we only get to see

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:07.540
as he dies in a woodchipper.

00:05:08.860 --> 00:05:11.580
"Tripping Motherf----- billies!"

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:13.840
X-Men Origins Deadpool

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:20.310
X-Men Origins: Wolverine is often considered
a low point for Deadpool fans, mostly because

00:05:20.310 --> 00:05:25.560
it turned the famously talkative Wade Wilson
into into a mouthless, murderous Mortal Kombat

00:05:25.560 --> 00:05:26.060
ripoff.

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:31.920
As much as you may hate that movie, Ryan Reynolds
has shown us that he probably hates it more,

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:34.480
parodying that movie’s action in Deadpool
2.

00:05:34.580 --> 00:05:38.919
If that wasn’t enough, he proved it once
and for all in the mid-credits sequence of

00:05:38.919 --> 00:05:44.710
Deadpool 2 when he used Cable's time travel
device to go back and fire bullet after bullet

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:46.700
into the earlier version of himself.

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:48.160
Flash Thompson

00:05:48.420 --> 00:05:53.440
The 800th issue of Amazing Spider-Man brought
fans a climactic battle between Spider-Man

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:58.220
and Norman Osborn, who had bonded with the
Carnage symbiote to form the Red Goblin.

00:05:58.610 --> 00:06:03.060
Osborn waged war on Peter Parker the way he
always had, by going after Spider-Man’s

00:06:03.060 --> 00:06:04.120
friends and family.

00:06:04.830 --> 00:06:09.340
Fortunately, Flash Thompson, Peter’s high
school bully turned close friend, was there

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:14.070
to help out with his abilities as the hero
Anti-Venom, using his power to neutralize

00:06:14.070 --> 00:06:19.360
shards of the Carnage symbiote that Osborn
had left behind in Aunt May, Mary Jane, and

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:20.800
Spidey’s other loved ones.

00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:22.840
His help came with a cost, though.

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:28.040
When Anti-Venom foiled Osborn’s contingency
plans, the Red Goblin’s retribution was

00:06:28.040 --> 00:06:29.400
swift and lethal.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:31.000
The Human Dynamo

00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:37.340
In Deathstroke #32, Slade Wilson goes to war
with Batman, but unsurprisingly, neither one

00:06:37.340 --> 00:06:38.540
of them is the one who dies.

00:06:38.889 --> 00:06:44.540
Instead, the Dark Knight tries to stop Wilson
from assassinating his latest target, an obscure

00:06:44.540 --> 00:06:47.310
hero named Ace Masterson: The Human Dynamo.

00:06:47.700 --> 00:06:48.300
The twist?

00:06:48.780 --> 00:06:53.660
It was actually Masterson himself who hired
Deathstroke, due to worries that the onset

00:06:53.660 --> 00:06:57.540
of dementia would make him too dangerous to
live with his explosive powers.

00:06:58.070 --> 00:07:02.440
Rather than find out for himself, he hired
Deathstroke to help him go out in a blaze

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:03.020
of glory.

00:07:03.540 --> 00:07:08.360
Batman tried to stop the hit from happening,
but eventually, Deathstroke just shot Masterson

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:08.860
in the head.

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:13.520
Pretty grim for a guy who used to be on a
team called the Justice Experience.

00:07:14.180 --> 00:07:15.020
Sinestro

00:07:15.500 --> 00:07:21.040
Sinestro isn't often considered a hero, but
in the ongoing comics tying into the Injustice

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:21.780
video games,

00:07:26.180 --> 00:07:30.220
the former villain rejoined the
Green Lantern Corps, just in time to fall

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:36.000
protecting Oa from an assault by Atrocitus,
the Red Lanterns, and a possessed Green Lantern

00:07:36.009 --> 00:07:38.389
Corps in Injustice 2 #64.

00:07:38.389 --> 00:07:43.640
And just to make things a little bit worse,
he was killed by his own daughter, Soranik,

00:07:44.100 --> 00:07:47.040
who then took up Sinestro’s ring as his
replacement.

00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:48.100
Triton

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:53.880
A series with a title like Death of the Inhumans
is bound to contain its share of dead superheroes,

00:07:53.880 --> 00:07:59.080
and the first came from Triton, one of the
original Inhumans who first appeared in 1965.

00:07:59.480 --> 00:08:03.620
While investigating a group of slaughtered
Inhumans who were murdered by their alien

00:08:03.620 --> 00:08:07.460
creators, the Kree, Triton discovers a bomb
hidden in a corpse.

00:08:08.040 --> 00:08:12.160
While the rest of the Inhumans are able to
teleport to safety, Triton’s not so lucky.

00:08:12.520 --> 00:08:16.320
He was the first Inhuman killed in the series,
but he would not be the last.

00:08:16.900 --> 00:08:17.620
Lockjaw

00:08:17.960 --> 00:08:22.000
Lockjaw is arguably the most beloved of all
Inhumans, for good reason.

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:24.800
He’s the goodest boy in the whole Marvel
Universe!

00:08:24.980 --> 00:08:28.300
C’mon, who doesn’t love a giant, teleporting
dog?

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:34.031
The answer, it seems, is a “super-Inhuman”
named Vox, the villain behind Death of the

00:08:34.031 --> 00:08:39.669
Inhumans, who has the powers of every other
Inhuman and wants nothing more than to destroy

00:08:39.669 --> 00:08:42.800
the whole group and their very large dog,
too.

00:08:43.180 --> 00:08:48.420
After Lockjaw rescues the often-villainous
Maximus the Mad from Vox, the two of them

00:08:48.420 --> 00:08:54.340
make one final stand… before they’re vaporized
when Vox uses Black Bolt’s devastating voice

00:08:54.340 --> 00:08:55.220
to destroy them.

00:08:55.780 --> 00:08:57.120
Hank Pym &amp; the van Dynes

00:08:57.400 --> 00:09:02.459
While most of Ant-Man and the Wasp takes place
before the events of Avengers: Infinity War,

00:09:02.460 --> 00:09:06.040
the post-credits scenes caught up to the Avengers'
battle with Thanos.

00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:11.560
In those, we learned that the original Ant-Man
and both women who went by the codename Wasp

00:09:11.570 --> 00:09:16.620
were victims of Thanos' infamous "snap,”
leaving Scott Lang floating in the Quantum

00:09:16.620 --> 00:09:18.580
Realm with what appears to be no way out.

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:20.000
Booster Gold

00:09:20.520 --> 00:09:26.800
Only two issues after Sinestro died defending
Oa, Injustice 2 #66 claimed another hero's

00:09:26.800 --> 00:09:28.180
life in its cosmic war.

00:09:29.220 --> 00:09:32.620
This time, though, it wasn’t the casualty
that the good guys thought it would be.

00:09:33.100 --> 00:09:38.300
While Blue Beetle was prepared to sacrifice
his life to stop Starro, Booster Gold made

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:40.800
a last-minute switch to keep the younger hero
alive.

00:09:41.270 --> 00:09:46.380
The last thing he saw was the second Blue
Beetle, Ted Kord, Ted had previously died

00:09:46.390 --> 00:09:50.990
himself, but was brought to Booster’s side
by time travel so that the two best friends

00:09:50.990 --> 00:09:53.380
could see each other in Booster’s final
moments.

00:09:54.300 --> 00:09:55.860
The Challengers of the Unknown

00:09:56.340 --> 00:10:00.640
Things in the miniseries New Challengers didn’t
take long to get pretty complicated, and the

00:10:00.640 --> 00:10:05.170
old school Challengers of the Unknown fell
victim to one of those complications.

00:10:05.170 --> 00:10:09.740
See if you can follow this one: New Challengers
#2 ended with the original team confronting

00:10:09.740 --> 00:10:13.120
their successors, and shooting their leader,
Prof, in the head.

00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:18.800
Since one of the original Challengers is named
Prof, they assumed this new one was an impostor,

00:10:19.120 --> 00:10:23.640
but he turned out to be a Prof from another
dimension with the surprising ability to recover

00:10:23.640 --> 00:10:25.140
from being shot in the head.

00:10:25.410 --> 00:10:29.720
To make matters even more complicated, the
original Challengers then encountered someone

00:10:29.720 --> 00:10:34.370
who they thought was the new Prof, only to
find a third prof... who turned out to be

00:10:34.370 --> 00:10:36.800
a murderous cybernetic mummy.

00:10:36.840 --> 00:10:37.840
Did you get all that?

00:10:38.100 --> 00:10:38.600
No!

00:10:38.600 --> 00:10:39.600
That's okay.

00:10:39.920 --> 00:10:43.080
Just remember Prof is dead… long live the
other Profs.

00:10:43.960 --> 00:10:44.640
Bloodstorm

00:10:44.960 --> 00:10:49.760
Hailing from an alternate reality where she
was bitten by Dracula, Bloodstorm is a vampiric

00:10:49.760 --> 00:10:52.470
version of the X-Men’s weather-controlling
Storm.

00:10:52.900 --> 00:10:57.660
More recently, she’s been serving on the
team in the core universe, but unfortunately,

00:10:57.660 --> 00:11:01.920
this led to her fighting against the mutant-hunting
Ahab in the pages of Extermination.

00:11:02.430 --> 00:11:07.320
Ahab came prepared, too, taking Bloodstorm
with a silver harpoon that he brought just

00:11:07.339 --> 00:11:09.779
in case a vampire X-Man showed up.

00:11:09.780 --> 00:11:14.480
It might seem unlikely that someone would
make preparations for that exact eventuality,

00:11:14.660 --> 00:11:16.380
but hey, it’s the Marvel Universe.

00:11:16.380 --> 00:11:18.060
That’s the sort of thing that happens a
lot.

00:11:18.860 --> 00:11:19.360
Cable

00:11:19.900 --> 00:11:24.720
The second mutant to fall in Extermination
was Cable, who was executed by a mysterious

00:11:24.720 --> 00:11:27.080
hooded figure who traveled back from the future.

00:11:27.360 --> 00:11:27.960
The twist?

00:11:28.420 --> 00:11:32.900
It turned out that Cable’s killer was a
younger, leaner version of Cable himself,

00:11:32.900 --> 00:11:36.500
who has set his sights on the time-traveling
original five X-Men.

00:11:37.460 --> 00:11:37.980
Nakia

00:11:38.220 --> 00:11:44.380
Fans of the MCU may remember Nakia as T'Challa's
love interest in 2017's Black Panther, where

00:11:44.380 --> 00:11:48.860
she was played by Lupita N’yong’o but
in the comics, she’s a very different character.

00:11:49.240 --> 00:11:55.380
Nakia was one of the first of the Dora Milaje
that readers met in 1998's Black Panther #1.

00:11:55.600 --> 00:12:01.580
Eventually, thanks partly to some meddling
from the demonic Mephisto, Nakia became obsessed

00:12:01.589 --> 00:12:07.220
with T'Challa and eventually left the Dora
Milaje, becoming a villain called Malice,

00:12:07.220 --> 00:12:08.440
powered by a mystical herb.

00:12:08.750 --> 00:12:13.440
In the Wakanda Forever event, we learn that
continued exposure to the herb that gave her

00:12:13.440 --> 00:12:15.600
powers is slowly killing Nakia

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:22.450
In Wakanda Forever: Avengers #1, Nakia reunited
with the Dora Milaje to defeat a Wakandan

00:12:22.450 --> 00:12:26.600
weapon called Mimic-27 that created doppelgängers
of superhumans.

00:12:27.230 --> 00:12:31.840
She convinced it to let go of the hatred it
felt for her sisters, and managed to release

00:12:31.840 --> 00:12:35.200
that same hatred from herself before succumbing
to the herb’s effects.

00:12:35.760 --> 00:12:40.080
She died, but was buried with honor among
other fallen Dora Milaje.

